From: SteamOS ARM alioth port
Subject: [PATCH] input: ft8756: let an unknown chip id through on request

The touch controller in this Redmi K40 answers the FocalTech SPI
protocol correctly -- the frames are framed where the driver expects
them, and the CRC16 the chip computes over its own reply (poly 0x8408)
matches the one the driver computes -- but it reports 0xef from
registers 0xA3 and 0x9F, and a boot id of 0x56b2 instead of 0x8756:

  read reg 0xa3 val_size 1 txlen 10 dp 7
  ft8756 rx: 02 02 02 02 02 02 02 ef 7e 10
  read reg 0x90 val_size 2 txlen 11 dp 7
  ft8756 rx: 02 02 02 02 02 02 02 56 b2 06 e1

alioth shipped with more than one touch supplier, so the reference
device this driver was written against is probably not the same part.
FocalTech parts share the point report format, so the rest of the
driver may still fit this one.

ft8756.ignore_id=1 is how to find out. Off by default: continuing past
an id the driver does not recognise means reading a register map that
may not be there.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/ft8756.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/ft8756.c
@@ -72,6 +72,20 @@
 module_param_named(debug, ft8756_debug_frames, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug, "dump raw SPI frames");
 
+/*
+ * ft8756.ignore_id=1: carry on when the chip answers with an id this
+ * driver does not know. The controller in this Redmi K40 answers the
+ * protocol correctly -- the frames are framed right and the CRC the
+ * chip computes over its own reply matches ours -- but reports 0xef
+ * from registers 0xA3 and 0x9F and a boot id of 0x56b2 rather than
+ * 0x8756. FocalTech parts share the point report format, so the rest
+ * of the driver may still fit. Off by default: a wrong guess here
+ * reads a foreign register map.
+ */
+static bool ft8756_ignore_id;
+module_param_named(ignore_id, ft8756_ignore_id, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ignore_id, "probe even when the chip id is unknown");
+
 struct ft8756_abs_object {
 	u16 x;
 	u16 y;
@@ -539,8 +553,11 @@
 
 skip_regulators:
 	ret = ft8756_check_chip_id(ts);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	if (ret) {
+		if (!ft8756_ignore_id)
+			return ret;
+		dev_warn(dev, "unknown chip id, continuing (ft8756.ignore_id=1)\n");
+	}
 
 	ret = ft8756_input_dev_config(ts);
 	if (ret) {
